+#
+# There is deliberately no policy for a *recoverable* generation failure, and
+# there should not be one. A generation that fails mid-batch on a runtime that
+# can still serve releases its batch entry and KV cache, keeps the worker, and
+# lets the next request through on the same process -- see `GET
